    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner response to expose `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. I implemented it in three well-separated pieces, mirroring the existing patterns in the codebase:\n\n1. **`util/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility utility holding just the standard Luhn algorithm (`checkDigit(String)`, ignoring non-digit characters like the code's hyphens). This sits alongside the other pure helpers (`TextNormalizer`, `RegistrationDatePolicy`).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 a derived getter `getCheckDigit()` that delegates to `Luhn.checkDigit(customerCode)`, returning `null` when no code is assigned. This matches how the other derived fields work (`getMembershipNumber`, `getLocality` \u2192 delegates to `Locality`), so no algorithm logic bloats the entity.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the Owner schema next to `membershipNumber`. The generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct maps it automatically from the matching `getCheckDigit()` getter \u2014 no mapper changes needed.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test (which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit) passes, and the full suite is green.",
